WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.821
In main, ready[s] is recorded after the input copy in copy’s stream. cudaStreamWaitEvent orders compute after that event, and process doubles the slot values.

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:17.631
Later, used[s] is recorded after the output copy; the next reuse waits for it.

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:21.499
Streams are ordered queues, and events connect their dependencies.

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:25.033
Copy and record ready.

00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:27.216
Finish supplying the slot’s input.

00:00:27.436 --> 00:00:28.737
Wait and compute.

00:00:28.957 --> 00:00:31.219
Order the kernel after its input event.

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:32.719
Record consumed.

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:35.904
Protect the slot until output copying finishes.

00:00:37.924 --> 00:00:46.095
Copy engines can transfer data while SMs execute independent kernels, if the device and workload support overlap.

00:00:46.315 --> 00:00:49.259
Streams express ordering, not dedicated hardware.

00:00:49.479 --> 00:00:54.897
A reusable buffer must wait for its previous consumer, even when its next copy is ready.
